# D125 pure center: actual collision and a conditional Pell obstruction

2026-09-07. **NO-GAIN for uniform pure-center exclusion.** There is an actual source-compatible mixed square/cube collision, so the first cubic residue cannot alone force V|C. Separately, an affine-unit parity lemma rules out a precise quadratic/Pell residue when its coefficients and regularity hypotheses hold. The missing arrow is deriving THAT quadratic residue from the complete moving-reference source, not proving the conditional algebra once it is supplied. No valuation bound on α, no all-ramification theorem and no guarded-source conclusion is claimed.

The incoming first-contact report `9b3538b8…` is still PROVISIONAL at this packet's cutoff. Its live gate was not read. This is the single authorized speculative generation. Accepted14c/f/g and the literal support/lift contract supply independent background; generic14p is not extrapolated to the exceptional zero fiber. Root supplied the uniform question and completed the projective divisor proof after this lane identified the possible Pell interface.

## 1. A genuine pure-source square/cube collision

Write

    R=p²V,  V=g³+p³−3p,  L=g+p,  r=pL²,
    C=r²−RL=3p³L(gL+1),
    D=rC/3,      W=C²L.

The equality for C follows from the degree-three identity V=L³−3p(gL+1). All of L,r,R lift ordinarily under φ(g)=v⁻¹, φ(p)=v⁴u−v−v⁻¹: φ(L)=v⁴u−v, and φ(r)=φ(p)φ(L)² has no pole. Thus C,D,W are ordinary as factored polynomial combinations. No full source powers are expanded.

The exact identities are

    9D²−C³ = C²(r²−C) = R C²L = RW.               (1)

Here C is even, degree6, weight−6 and origin order4; D is odd, degree9, weight−3 and origin order7. C has zero constant/p⁸ coefficients and is not divisible by V: modulo the irreducible V it equals r², while V divides neither p nor L. These are actual source-compatible coefficients, not only a formal R=g analogy. The divisor V is irreducible by the already charged valuation1/3 cubic argument.

As a single countercontrol for the first pole mechanism, over K[s]/(s⁷), set k=0 and use the FACTORED presentation

    A=R³+s²RC+s³D,
    B=R⁵+(5/3)s²R³C+(5/3)s³R²D
       +(5/9)s⁴RC²+(10/9)s⁵CD+(5/81)s⁶W.          (2)

The formal five-thirds coefficient identity and (1) give [A,B]=0 modulo s⁷. This is one algebraic collision construction, not a sequence of next-digit searches. The script verifies the identity on the small formal specialization R=g,r=p,L=1; substitution of the proved polynomial circuit identity (1) establishes the general formula.

Every positive A component has degree≤11 and weight≤−3; every positive B component has degree≤21 and weight≤−1. More precisely the five displayed B correction degrees are21,19,17,15,13 and weights−3,−1,−11,−9,−7. They lie strictly below the fixed faces. A's additional edge i≤2j is preserved: r has maximal i−2j equal0 and C has−3. Ordinaryness follows from L,r,R, and every correction has origin order≥7, so x=y=e=[p]A=0. Hence (2) obeys ALL unguarded source support, face, lift and saturated low rows at this precision, not merely its displayed Jacobian subset. The optional whole B₁₅ slice is achieved by subtracting [p¹⁵]B times the entire A.

The references are h=α=0. Thus the first-contact mixed product and low equations are respected. Nevertheless k is ZERO in this nilpotent coefficient algebra: this is neither a nonzero-k arc nor a point of the guarded ring. No extension beyond this precision is asserted or tested. It shows precisely that a source-compatible mixed D can absorb the first C³/R pole; it does not show that arbitrary α/h corrections are harmless or that a later double pole can be removed.

## 2. Every affine unit on V is even

Work over an algebraically closed characteristic-zero field; a contradiction after scalar extension also applies over the original field. The projective closure

    E: g³+p³−3pz²=0

is smooth: the three partial derivatives force g=0, p²=z² and pz=0, hence no projective singular point. It is integral by the preceding irreducibility argument. The involution σ:[g:p:z]→[−g:−p:z] fixes each of the three points at infinity z=0 and fixes the affine origin O.

For a unit u in K[g,p]/(V), its divisor on E is supported at those infinity points. Therefore div(σ(u)/u)=0. The ratio is a global invertible regular function on the smooth projective curve and is constant. The standard global-function input is [Stacks Lemma33.9.3(8)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0366); its whole statement and proof were read directly, with earlier cohomology dependencies imported. Since u(O)≠0 and σ(O)=O, the constant is1. Thus

    σ(u)=u for every affine unit u.                 (U)

This does NOT say all units are constant. The checker supplies a nonconstant even unit and its actual polynomial inverse. If ω²+ω+1=0 and L_i=g+ω^i p, then

    L₀/L₁ = 1+(1−ω)L₀L₂/3

is regular and invertible on V; the analogous reversed ratio is its inverse. Exact reduction modulo V and ω²+ω+1 verifies their product1. Thus the proof uses parity, not an incorrect trivial-unit-group assumption.

## 3. Conditional quadratic/Pell discriminator

Let C,D be REGULAR elements of K[g,p]/(V), with C even and D odd, and let a,b be scalar constants. Suppose

    D²=C(aC+b).                                    (P)

If a≠0 and b≠0, choose √a over Kbar. The two regular elements

    U_±=2aC+b±2√a D

have product b², so both are affine units. By (U) both are even, while σ exchanges them. Hence D=0 and C is a scalar, either0 or−b/a. If C(O)=0, only C=0 remains.

If a≠0,b=0, direct factorization D²=aC² in the integral domain gives D=±√a C; parity forces C=D=0. If a=0,b≠0, no such obstruction follows: C=D²/b is allowed. If a=b=0, only D=0 follows and even C is unrestricted. These branches are not silently localized away.

The regularity hypothesis is essential to the unit argument: arbitrary rational residues with affine poles need not give units. No source-derived coefficient is declared regular on V without a literal construction or cleared-denominator proof.

## 4. The exact missing source arrow

The rederived moving-reference identity remains

    [A,B]=[R_s,(3R_s²+α)G−δF−(5/3)R_sF²]+[F,G].

In particular α(s)G, δ(s)F, the moving R_s and the cross bracket remain present. The checker rejects deleting αG from the ACTUAL identity. The first-contact information only controls F_j=RC, normalized δ through j, and

    ord(αh)>j,   ord(x)>j,
    x²=3ky,      y=−h³+αt.

It does not license F_p=0, positive-origin bounds for every formal-root coefficient, or suppression of possible cancellation in y. Lower scalar α motion may compete with mixed remainders before the generic3j collision; polynomial centralizer corrections and moving denominators must be accounted for at their actual valuations.

No proof here derives (P), with scalar a≠0 and REGULAR C,D, as the complete earliest residue of an arbitrary source arc. In particular, **ord(α)≥j is NOT proved**. The actual cubic collision (1), 9D²=C³ modulo V, is not a quadratic/Pell relation and survives. The conditional Pell lemma identifies a potentially decisive interface, but the arrow from full source to that interface is still missing.

