## 2. Unit parity: CONFIRMED

E: g³+p³−3pz²=0. Its Jacobian generators J₁=3g², J₂=3p²−3z², J₃=−6pz satisfy g²=J₁/3, p³=pJ₂/3−zJ₃/6, z³=−zJ₂/3−pJ₃/6 (checked), so the singular locus is empty in P²; E is a smooth plane cubic, hence integral (V is also absolutely irreducible by the charged valuation-1/3 argument). At z=0, g³+p³=L₀L₁L₂ over ω²+ω+1=0 gives three distinct points [−ω^i:1:0], each fixed individually by σ because [−g:−p:0]=[g:p:0]; σ preserves E (σF=−F) and fixes O=(0,0)∈V. For a unit u of K[g,p]/(V), u and u⁻¹ are regular off the P_i, so div u is supported on the P_i; σ*div u=div u pointwise, so σ(u)/u has divisor zero and is a global section of O_E. Stacks Lemma 33.9.3(8) (whole statement and proof read; snapshot in the box, SHA256 `86133e93…`) gives Γ(E,O_E)=K for E proper and geometrically integral over K=Kbar; (8) follows from (7) via (1)–(4), importing Cohomology of Schemes 30.19.2 and 30.5.2 and Algebra 10.53.2, 10.60.7, 10.25.1, 10.44.2, 10.44.4. Evaluating at the fixed affine origin gives the constant u(O)/u(O)=1. Over a subfield K the identity descends because K[g,p]/(V) injects into Kbar[g,p]/(V). The primary note is a faithful paraphrase. Nonconstant even unit: U=L₀/L₁=1+(1−ω)L₀L₂/3 with inverse 1+(ω−1)L₁L₂/3; checked U·Uinv=1 and L₁U=L₀ modulo (V,ω²+ω+1) using L₀L₁L₂=3p on V; its normal form has seven terms, is even, σ-fixed, and U(O)=1 (divisor 2P₀−2P₁). Controls: U+g and the changed scalar 1/2 fail; the odd regular L₀ is σ-anti-invariant and vanishes at O, so the lemma is genuinely about units, not all regular functions.

## 3. Conditional Pell lemma: CONFIRMED

With a=(√a)², U_±=2aC+b±2√aD satisfy U₊U₋=b²−4a(D²−C(aC+b)) and U₊−U₋=4√aD, and D→−D exchanges them (checked). Retained hypotheses: scalar a,b; C,D regular in the domain K[g,p]/(V); C even, D odd. a≠0,b≠0: both U_± are units, hence even by §2, hence equal, so D=0 and C(aC+b)=0 gives C∈{0,−b/a}; C(O)=0 leaves C=0. a≠0,b=0: D²=aC²=(D−√aC)(D+√aC) with parity forces D=C=0. a=0,b≠0: C=p²/b, D=p is an even/odd regular solution, so no obstruction. a=b=0: D=0 only. A residue with affine poles gives no unit, so regularity is load-bearing.

